diff --git a/docs/deploy.md b/docs/deploy.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..247c45b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deploy.md
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+## Deploying Fizzy
+
+Fizzy runs on one Linux server: Docker, SQLite, background jobs, and HTTPS from kamal-proxy, all in a single container.
+
+Someone who forks this repo should fill in their hostname, mail server, and secrets, run `kamal setup`, and have Fizzy at `https://their-host`. Data lives on a Docker volume so it survives the next deploy.
+
+### Prerequisites
+
+- A Linux server you can SSH into (root or a user that can run Docker)
+- Docker on the machine you deploy from (Kamal builds the image there)
+- A hostname with a DNS record pointing at the server (ports 80 and 443 open)
+- An SMTP server - Fizzy signs people in with magic-link email
+
+### 1. Fill in your hostname and mail server
+
+Edit `config/deploy.yml`:
+
+- `servers.web` - SSH hostname or IP of the box
+- `proxy.host` and `APP_HOST` - public hostname (Fizzy will be at `https://that-host`)
+- `SMTP_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_PORT`, `SMTP_USERNAME`, `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS` - your mail server
+
+### 2. Fill in secrets
+
+Edit `.kamal/secrets` (or export the values in your environment):
+
+- `SECRET_KEY_BASE` - generate once with `bin/rails secret` and keep it stable
+- `SMTP_PASSWORD` - mail server password (empty if the server allows unauthenticated relay)
+
+### 3. Setup
+
+From the app root:
+
+```sh
+kamal setup
+```
+
+That installs Docker on the server if needed, builds the image, boots kamal-proxy with Let's Encrypt, prepares the database, and starts Fizzy. Solid Queue runs inside Puma, so background jobs run on the box.
+
+SQLite files and uploads are stored in the `fizzy_storage` volume at `/rails/storage`. They survive container replacements.
+
+Later deploys:
+
+```sh
+kamal deploy
+```
+
+### Optional
+
+- Web Push: set `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` (see the [Development guide](development.md)).
+- Authenticated registry: set `registry.username` / `password` and `KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD`.
+- ARM servers: set `builder.arch` to `arm64`.
diff --git a/test/lib/deploy_config_test.rb b/test/lib/deploy_config_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2d65184
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/lib/deploy_config_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+require "test_helper"
+require "yaml"
+require "erb"
+
+class DeployConfigTest < ActiveSupport::TestCase
+  setup do
+    rendered = ERB.new(File.read(Rails.root.join("config/deploy.yml")), trim_mode: "-").result
+    @config = YAML.safe_load(rendered, aliases: true)
+  end
+
+  test "deploys one web box with SSL from the proxy" do
+    assert_equal [ "192.168.0.1" ], @config.dig("servers", "web")
+    assert_nil @config.dig("servers", "job")
+    assert_nil @config.dig("servers", "jobs")
+    assert_equal true, @config.dig("proxy", "ssl")
+    assert_equal "app.example.com", @config.dig("proxy", "host")
+  end
+
+  test "persists sqlite and uploads on a volume and runs jobs in puma" do
+    assert_includes @config["volumes"], "fizzy_storage:/rails/storage"
+    assert_equal true, @config.dig("env", "clear", "SOLID_QUEUE_IN_PUMA")
+  end
+
+  test "asks for hostname, mail server, and secrets" do
+    assert_equal "app.example.com", @config.dig("env", "clear", "APP_HOST")
+    assert_equal "smtp.example.com", @config.dig("env", "clear", "SMTP_ADDRESS")
+    assert_includes @config.dig("env", "secret"), "SECRET_KEY_BASE"
+    assert_includes @config.dig("env", "secret"), "SMTP_PASSWORD"
+  end
+end
